# TradingView Simple MTF Trend Breakout

## Source
- Source: [[sources/tradingview-mechanical-strategy-scripts]]
- Page / Timestamp: TradingView script `Simple Trend & Breakout System v6`, author handle `shitholed`, open-source strategy, accessed 2026-05-22, page shows Apr 10 and updated May 2, https://www.tradingview.com/script/plDp6ZIw/

## Mechanics

### Entry
Use H4/D1 baseline:

- Compute EMA(240) anchored to D1 as the MTF trend filter.
- Long context: close > D1 EMA(240).
- Short context: close < D1 EMA(240).
- Bullish momentum signal: configurable number of consecutive higher closes, P2 default 3.
- Bearish momentum signal: configurable number of consecutive lower closes, P2 default 3.
- Long stop order = signal candle high * 1.001.
- Short stop order = signal candle low * 0.999.
- Cancel pending order if not filled within 3 bars or if trend context flips.

### Exit
- Source exit is a dynamic percentage trailing stop.
- P2 baseline trailing stop distance = 2.5%.
- Close long when price crosses below trailing stop.
- Close short when price crosses above trailing stop.

### Stop Loss
- Initial stop is the same 2.5% trailing stop from entry, then trails only in the favorable direction.
- V5 fallback hard stop = ATR(14) * 2.5 if 2.5% is wider than 3 ATR.
- No fixed target; exit is trail-only.

### Position Sizing
V5 default: fixed-risk $1,000 for P2 baseline, one position per symbol/magic.

### Zusatzliche Filter
- Use closed bars for higher/lower close sequence.
- Daily EMA must use non-repainting HTF data.
- Disable date-range/stat-table features; they are report utilities, not trading rules.

## Concepts (what kind of strategy is this)
- [[concepts/breakout]] - enters on stop order beyond the signal candle.
- [[concepts/trend-following]] - trades only with D1 EMA trend context.
- [[concepts/trailing-stop]] - management uses a dynamic trailing stop.

